/**

@page page_peano_runtime_analysis Runtime analysis

\tableofcontents

Peano applications report global grid, memory, rank-partition, and subtree-task
statistics after program steps. The Grid Snapshot presents the latest
synchronised view across all ranks.

# Grid

The grid section reports leaf and refined cells, persistent and hanging
vertices, and the minimum and maximum grid levels. These counts describe the
global logical grid. The replicated structural cells that reach the local
subtrees are reported separately as decomposition overhead.

# Inter-rank decomposition

`MPI Load Balance` compares the average owned leaf count with the most loaded
rank and prints the minimum and maximum leaves per rank. `Spine Replication`
reports replicated structural cells relative to owned cells and gives the
minimum and maximum replicated counts per rank.

A low balance value identifies unequal geometric ownership. High spine
replication identifies a small local workload relative to the replicated
coarse structure and rank interfaces.

# Intra-rank decomposition

`Subtree Tasks` gives the global task count and its range per rank. `Cells per
Task` gives the smallest, largest, and mean number of cells. `Thread Ceiling`
estimates the best utilisation permitted by the largest task, while the phase
report line `Utilisation` measures the task time accumulated during the latest
sweep against its wall-clock task window.

A high ceiling with low measured utilisation points to scheduling,
dependencies, communication waits, memory bandwidth, or serial work outside
the subtree tasks. A low ceiling identifies insufficient or uneven task
decomposition.

# Regridding

The dynamic-AMR report records the leaf count, level range, MPI load balance,
subtree tasks, and thread ceiling before and after a drain. It also reports
the number and duration of the sweeps needed to settle the topology.

@ref page_peano_performance_optimisation provides tuning guidance.

*/
